{"c":[{"id":"606474285b004d9e","sum":"B14-B15 executor: stopReason on stops; stop/takeOver revokes grants at once; acts only under actGrants; wait for Chrome's late web AX; walk checks catch silent drops (Chrome AXSelectedText, bg WKWebView). A10: gate skips whole-display overlays; filled field caret at bottom.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"e5e5e527a27f6c88","sum":"B14-B15 executor: stopped progress carries stopReason; stop/takeOver revokes the grant at once; wait for Chrome's late web AX fields before acting. Run an oracle-Jev replay copy before live replays.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d0f5d3ab6d535ae7","sum":"B14: a stopped taskProgress carries stopReason (stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase). Before a live replay, run an oracle-Jev copy of live-replay.ts to see withholding and wrong fills for free.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T100919Z-9bbdea6cd359a808","text":"A stopped taskProgress must carry stopReason: executor progress() refuses 'stopped' at type level and stops go through stopped(reason); TaskProgress is a zod union on phase so the exported JSON Schema states the rule (B14).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T100919Z-aefa98c201821a3a","text":"Before a live replay, copy live-replay.ts with an oracle Jev (gold if offered, else a name-like decoy) to see withholding and wrong fills for free; B14's copy is ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b14/oracle/oracle-replay.ts.txt.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"166b843e5f81c9fe","sum":"Stop or takeOver revokes the act grant at once (fakes refuse ungranted acts only with enforceGrants). Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds late: wait for the form's fields in the screen model before acting, or plans stop target-not-found (B15).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124042Z-0ff3662999b3099a","text":"A stop or takeOver revokes the task's act grant at once, so a write still on its way is refused and the run ends as stopped by you; test fakes (FakeApp, SocketReader) refuse acts without a grant only when enforceGrants is set.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124042Z-b3569a4cf63d6bee","text":"Chrome builds its web AX tree seconds after the reader asks for it: wait until the form's fields are in the screen model before acting, or the first plans stop with target-not-found (B15 explore run).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0334cdaad96cb7e2","sum":"B15: acts only under helper actGrants; Chrome no-ops AXSelectedText, background WKWebView drops writes, the walk check catches it. A10: gate skips whole-display elevated windows (Snipaste); a filled single-line field's caret sits at its bottom edge.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ead499ab30c4256f","sum":"B15: caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (120 s max; --act-pids for fixtures; only accepted offers get grants). Chrome takes AXValue but no-ops AXSelectedText; background WKWebView drops writes silently; TextEdit takes all; the walk check catches drops.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124106Z-598a6c678d777d69","text":"caret-screen acts only under a helper actGrant (task, pid, window; 120 s max, monotonic); --act-pids is for fixture tests. Only accepted offers get grants (Executor.run opts.grant); a consumer runPlan never does, so the product refuses it (B15).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124106Z-77698db11d4c9d42","text":"Real targets (B15): Chrome takes AXValue on web inputs, front or back, but answers AXSelectedText ok and changes nothing; WKWebView in background-only caret-fixture drops value and insert silently; TextEdit takes all. The executor's walk check caught each drop.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5b3a9b25ba5ddf8e","sum":"A10: SurfaceGate skips elevated windows covering a whole display (Snipaste's layer-25 one) or every offer is held covered; KeyType puts a filled single-line field's caret at its bottom edge, so fit checks add no height below the caret.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124605Z-cfb4c770396b2ce0","text":"Snipaste keeps a layer-25 alpha-1 window around the main display; SurfaceGate skips elevated windows containing a whole display, or every offer is held as covered (A10).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T124605Z-ed64edafa04a21d4","text":"KeyType estimates a single-line field's caret flush with the field's bottom edge once it holds text; fit checks must not add height below the caret (A10 cd92606).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4c884d385d74c3d7","sum":"A10-A12/B15-B16: foreground runs lose the front to Playwright windows and can't beat T3 Code; host-only memory contracts (add, uses, ops) in Fixtures/memory.ndjson; renders need EntryField/ScrollingColumn; rebundle the fixture after builds.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"23c2af1ea7cc2a6a","sum":"Foreground runs lose the front to other runs' Playwright windows (20-50 s) and fixture 'activate legacy' can't beat T3 Code. Host-only memory contracts live in Fixtures/memory.ndjson; renders use EntryField/ScrollingColumn (A10-A11, B15).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"577149bb4f331439","sum":"Foreground runs: other runs' Playwright WebKit windows grab the front every 20-50 s (start right after one quits, A10); caret-fixture's 'activate legacy' can't take the front from T3 Code. Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes, so no insert fallback there (B15).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T124605Z-ffdb92be588e7494","text":"Other runs' Playwright WebKit windows take the foreground every 20-50 s; on-screen runs started right after one quits (A10 onscreen-try.sh) or they fail as appNotFront.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T135628Z-a8acf778077d3916","text":"Chrome ignores AXSelectedTextRange writes on web inputs (selection stays 0+0), so the insert fallback is refused there; and caret-fixture's 'activate legacy' cannot take the front from T3 Code, only from apps the eval launched (B15).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9390cf8f12481e1c","sum":"A11: host-only memory contracts (add op, permission uses) live in Tests/CaretHostCoreTests/Fixtures/memory.ndjson; typed values wait in MemoryBook. ImageRenderer can't draw TextField/ScrollView: use EntryField and ScrollingColumn, which draw stand-ins off screen.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T141909Z-1887ef6a0983e76b","text":"Helper memoryRequest has no add op and records no permission uses; the host's contract for both is apps/caret/Tests/CaretHostCoreTests/Fixtures/memory.ndjson, and typed values wait in MemoryBook (memory only) until a helper accepts add (A11).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T141909Z-b0300a8600af9266","text":"ImageRenderer cannot draw TextField or ScrollView: Caret windows use EntryField and ScrollingColumn (Design/EntryField.swift), which draw still stand-ins when Gallery.png sets rendersOffscreen (A11).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"8aaa9c3b690ffacb","sum":"Rerun bundle-fixture.sh after fixture builds; desk scripts reading offers().at(-1) move the desk a day (IGNORED_LIMIT 2). Onboarding's know step needs a memoryReply list naming 'add' in ops (host contract); hidden until the helper sends it.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"71c6eaf6da7b9131","sum":"Desk scripts reading offers().at(-1) across sittings move the desk a day (gate IGNORED_LIMIT 2 holds a third walked-past offer). Rerun bundle-fixture.sh after any fixture build, or evals exec the old CaretFixture.app (B16).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T141909Z-f52622867dbc213f","text":"Desk scripts that read offers(...).at(-1) across sittings must move the desk a day and require a new offer: two walked-past offers in one app a day are held (gate.ts IGNORED_LIMIT 2), so .at(-1) silently reads the previous offer (A11).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T145037Z-c765ed8386dc228d","text":"Evals exec CaretFixture.app, a copy of caret-fixture made by apps/screen-reader/scripts/bundle-fixture.sh: rerun it after every swift build that changes the fixture, or the eval runs the old one (B16 lost two planner cases to an 08:33 bundle).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"30d8beae6ea2a379","sum":"Onboarding's know step shows only when a memoryReply list names op add in 'ops' (host contract, memory.ndjson); until the helper sends ops, the step stays hidden (A12).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261003T155259Z-0e3686f311fbff4b","text":"Onboarding's know step shows only when a memoryReply list carries ops naming add (host contract, Tests/CaretHostCoreTests/Fixtures/memory.ndjson); today's helper sends no ops, so the step is hidden until B17 adds the op and the ops field (A12).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261003T155327Z-6557f0a64fa5989e","text":"Onboarding's know step shows only when a memoryReply list names op add in 'ops' (host contract, memory.ndjson). Today's helper sends no ops, so the step stays hidden until the screen track adds the op and the field (A12).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
